1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,440
So ChatGPT now has an additional functionality

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:03,940
called Scheduled Tasks.

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:06,540
This allows you to set up recurring work,

4
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,180
whether it be daily or weekly,

5
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,160
so that you can automate some of your day-to-day activities

6
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,360
using ChatGPT.

7
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,080
To utilise this feature, what you need to do

8
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,340
is go into the top left,

9
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:18,240
and then click on GPT-4o with Scheduled Tasks.

10
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:22,360
Could say, let's create a task every day

11
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:25,320
to make a social media post

12
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:30,240
for my data engineering consultancy.

13
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:39,360
I want to make a new post at 8am every day.

14
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,300
And then ChatGPT task is gonna realise

15
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,000
that this is a task that needs to be done.

16
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:45,900
So you can see it says, create a task,

17
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:50,520
and it's going to remind us every day at 8am.

18
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:51,820
If you click on the triple dots,

19
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:54,540
you can either pause the task, edit the task,

20
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:56,500
and you can see this is the name of the task.

21
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,500
The instructions tell me to make a social media post,

22
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:01,040
and we could also say,

23
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:05,780
we could change this to generate a social media post

24
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:08,560
for my data engineering consultancy.

25
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:10,100
You can change the schedule

26
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,820
to daily, weekly, monthly, annually, or custom.

27
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:14,420
And then as well as that,

28
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,680
the other thing you'll want to do to activate this

29
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:20,400
is make sure that you have desktop notifications turned on.

30
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:21,920
So remember to click allow there.

31
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:23,620
Your notifications are turned on.

32
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,500
Also, the other place you'll need to go

33
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:26,960
to see all of your tasks

34
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:29,220
is go on your profile icon in the top right,

35
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:31,440
click on that, go to tasks in beta,

36
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:33,500
and then you can see these are all the tasks

37
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,880
that you've got where you can pause or delete a task,

38
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,020
or you can edit a task as well there.
